    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.48 from 5 h onward, which could have been detector saturation. I diluted the 18 h aliquot to test that. At 10x the two replicates read 0.0491 and 0.0472, which scales to about 0.48. At 3x the three replicates read 0.1761, 0.1632 and 0.1622, which scales to about 0.49–0.53. Both match the undiluted value of 0.4885 within replicate noise, so the reader responds proportionally at this density. If the reader were saturating, the diluted samples would scale to a clearly higher OD. The culture appears to have reached stationary phase at about 0.48."
